WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.991
Main runs on the CPU.

00:00:02.171 --> 00:00:06.235
It starts with a one element NumPy array
containing zero.

00:00:06.415 --> 00:00:11.256
To device copies that value into a separate
array in GPU memory.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.400
The first one in the square brackets
requests one block.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.401
The second one requests one thread per
block.

00:00:18.581 --> 00:00:24.536
A streaming multiprocessor, or S M, is a
part of the GPU chip that executes the

00:00:24.536 --> 00:00:24.908
thread.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.622
The thread writes forty-two to the GPU
array.

00:00:28.802 --> 00:00:31.995
The original CPU array still contains zero.

00:00:32.175 --> 00:00:35.541
Which line makes the new value available on
the CPU?

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.144
Copy to host waits for the result and
returns a CPU array.

00:00:40.324 --> 00:00:42.298
Main can now print forty-two.

00:00:42.478 --> 00:00:47.842
Change the assignment to seventy-three and
trace the same steps with the new value.
